   This lemma implies that if X is a smooth affine variety with Pic (X) = 0
and Γ(X, OX )∗ = C∗ , then an étale endomorphism ϕ : X → X is almost
surjective. This is, in particular, the case for X = An . Let f : Y → X be
a Galois affine pseudo-covering of smooth affine varieties with Galois group
G := Gal(C(Y )/C(X)) and let Ye be the normalization of X in C(Y ). Then
Y is a Zariski open set of Ye and the group G acts freely on Ye so that X =
Ye /G. The purity of branch loci implies that the normalization morphism
fe : Ye → X is a finite étale morphism and that Ye is thereby smooth.
